        ],
        "abstract": "Any successful founder of a technology-based company can tell you, with an ethereal smile, exactly when and where \"the big idea\" hit him. Then his expression will flash to a serious battle-worn stare as he explains all the work he had to do to get his product launched. The intellectual property (IP) aspects of a typical odyssey from startup to product release requires one to go beyond the \"eureka moment\" and ask if you have discovered a viable \"big idea\".",
